rec.games.hack's own dz@cornu.ucsb.edu (Daniel James Zerkle) said:
-This 3.0 is driving me nuts.  Wizards are too wimpy to survive
-the first few levels.   Priest do ok at first, but I can't get
-them past the seventh level.  The battle-hardy characters do well
-in the first few levels, but they can't cast spells worth a damn,
-so they don't do so well when it really counts.  I still haven't
-figured out what to do with with healers, archeologists, or tourists.

I've had the most difficult times with Wizards (unless I get some good
starting magic) and with Elves (their abilities are more suited for lower
levels).  

Tourists do ok throwing darts and using the camera.  The credit card is a 
handy thing too...let no chest go unlooted.

The bullwhip that archeologists is a really good weapon.  Don't switch for
a while.  You may also notice that Archeologists can tell the difference
between gems and glass.  Handy, eh?

<Potential Spoiler for Healers>


Note that you're given *all* those potions of healing.  Quaff 'em all, first
chance you get.  You stand a much better chance of surviving when you've got
25-31 h.p. at first level than 12 or 13.  Use that wand of sleep to kill a
goblin.  The scalpel has got to be one of the wimpiest weapons you'll find.
And wear armor.  Any armor.  All you can.  And keep your pet until you can
take care of yourself.

I've never done spectacular with a healer, but then I don't have the patience
to do so.  It shouldn't require too much luck.

